  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive).\n\nCOMPOUND VERB: {話|はな}す (to speak) + かける (to initiate action toward)\n\nCONJUGATION (ichidan): {話|はな}しかける → {話|はな}しかけない → {話|はな}しかけた → {話|はな}しかけて\n\nPATTERN: 〜に{話|はな}しかける (speak to ~)\n\nNUANCE: Emphasizes the act of initiating conversation, rather than simply talking. Often implies the other person wasn't expecting to be addressed.\n\nThe 〜かける pattern indicates the beginning of an action directed toward someone/something.",
